Note: QUICK-260504-cks — runtime (chord String) constructor + expanded vocabulary
use "std.flow"

Note: === Triads ===
(print (str (chord "C")))
(print (str (chord "Cmaj")))
(print (str (chord "CM")))
(print (str (chord "Cm")))
(print (str (chord "Cmin")))
(print (str (chord "Cdim")))
(print (str (chord "Caug")))

Note: === Power chord (5) ===
Note: lexer-form C5 stays as a NOTE; string-form is the power chord
(print (str (chord "C5")))
(print (str (chord "G5")))

Note: === Sixths ===
(print (str (chord "C6")))
(print (str (chord "Cm6")))
(print (str (chord "C69")))
(print (str (chord "C6/9")))
(print (str (chord "Cm69")))

Note: === Sevenths ===
(print (str (chord "C7")))
(print (str (chord "Cdom7")))
(print (str (chord "Cmaj7")))
(print (str (chord "CM7")))
(print (str (chord "Cm7")))
(print (str (chord "Cmin7")))
(print (str (chord "Cdim7")))
(print (str (chord "Cm7b5")))
(print (str (chord "Cm7f5")))
(print (str (chord "CmMaj7")))

Note: === Sus + 7 ===
(print (str (chord "Csus2")))
(print (str (chord "Csus4")))
(print (str (chord "Csus")))
(print (str (chord "C7sus4")))
(print (str (chord "C7sus2")))
(print (str (chord "C9sus4")))

